@@ -27,9 +27,16 @@ One execution of a Job.
 A Run has a stable id and one terminal outcome:
 
 - succeeded;
-- failed.
+- failed;
+- cancelled.
 
-A Run may contain one or more Attempts.
+A Run may contain zero or more Attempts.
+
+An operator may cancel a running Run, including while it is awaiting a retry.
+A cancelled Run accepts no further Attempts. Cancelling it again succeeds
+without changing it; cancelling a succeeded or failed Run is a conflict.
+Cancellation preserves existing Attempts and Alerts and emits no new Alert.
+The Dashboard includes cancelled Runs when displaying a Job's Last result.
 
